WEBVTT

00:01:42.060 --> 00:01:42.560
"ELECTION TIME BEGINS!"

00:01:42.890 --> 00:01:46.230
Election season is now in full swing.

00:01:46.230 --> 00:01:49.730
The approval ratings at the time of announcement,
as reported by the school newspaper,

00:01:49.730 --> 00:01:54.570
had Yokuya at the top
just like Mr. Senpai predicted.

00:01:54.570 --> 00:02:00.570
I don't know how that un-individualistic classmate
gathered support or from which demographic,

00:02:00.570 --> 00:02:03.620
"YUBIWA ACADEMY STUDENT COUNCIL
PRESIDENTIAL ELECTIONS WHO WILL YOU VOTE FOR?"

00:02:00.570 --> 00:02:03.620
but as a result of
an impartial questionnaire,

00:02:03.620 --> 00:02:09.210
"YUBIWA ACADEMY STUDENT COUNCIL
PRESIDENTIAL ELECTIONS WHO WILL YOU VOTE FOR?"

00:02:03.620 --> 00:02:09.210
a majority answered that
they'll "vote for Kinshiro Yokuya."

00:02:09.210 --> 00:02:11.790
In any case, as opposed to Yokuya,

00:02:11.790 --> 00:02:16.590
Mayumi Dojima was in third place
on the approval questionnaire.

00:02:16.590 --> 00:02:20.050
"MAYUMI DOJIMA
A SHINING VISION"

00:02:16.590 --> 00:02:20.050
But she was putting up a good fight.

00:02:39.530 --> 00:02:43.160
When I actually live days
without getting run over like today,

00:02:43.160 --> 00:02:49.960
it feels like it's too much of a stretch to think that
Naganawa was targeted when she got run over.

00:02:49.960 --> 00:02:57.670
Fortunately her case wasn't serious in the end,
but Naganawa could have also died.

00:02:57.670 --> 00:03:00.050
Even if they wanted
to make it look like an accident,

00:03:00.050 --> 00:03:02.680
there must have been other methods.

00:03:02.680 --> 00:03:06.140
Let's say that the "hit-and-run driver
of D Hill" actually exists,

00:03:06.140 --> 00:03:10.190
but the mystery remains of why
a car was chosen as the weapon.

00:03:10.190 --> 00:03:14.150
Well, even if there was an assassin who had
relations with the school administration,

00:03:14.150 --> 00:03:19.860
it's not like my election would be guaranteed
by exposing this scheme to the public's eye.

00:03:20.820 --> 00:03:21.950
Ouch, ouch, ouch!

00:03:21.950 --> 00:03:25.120
Sorry! I'm sorry.
It's bad to lose heart, right?

00:03:25.120 --> 00:03:26.240
Mayu.

00:03:26.290 --> 00:03:27.040
"MA"

00:03:27.040 --> 00:03:27.620
"YU"

00:03:27.950 --> 00:03:29.200
Mayu.

00:03:29.200 --> 00:03:31.620
You're overlooking something important.

00:03:33.330 --> 00:03:37.210
If you're thinking about why a car was
chosen as the weapon to be a mystery,

00:03:37.210 --> 00:03:39.970
a detective must solve that mystery.

00:03:39.970 --> 00:03:42.800
Something that's unnatural
always has its reasons for being so.

00:03:42.800 --> 00:03:45.180
About the car, and...

00:03:47.430 --> 00:03:49.560
about Kinshiro Yokuya.

00:03:50.680 --> 00:03:53.480
"THE DELINQUENT BODYGUARD"
If you're using a car as the weapon,

00:03:53.480 --> 00:03:56.270
is there any merit to that
besides making it look like an accident?

00:03:57.360 --> 00:04:00.320
A new eyewitness isn't going to show up,

00:04:00.320 --> 00:04:03.700
and it's not like you'll get
a statement along those lines.

00:04:03.700 --> 00:04:08.290
And there wasn't any trouble like that
around Naganawa, either.

00:04:08.290 --> 00:04:09.790
To be blunt...

00:04:11.080 --> 00:04:12.160
Well...

00:04:13.670 --> 00:04:18.920
If I say this, Nagahiro might get pissed,
so I don't really want to say it.

00:04:18.920 --> 00:04:22.380
Well, Nagahiro getting pissed
is ultimately out of our control,

00:04:22.380 --> 00:04:25.800
but it's not an idea that
our leader would like.

00:04:27.100 --> 00:04:29.390
That's the problem.

00:04:29.390 --> 00:04:30.600
What I mean is,

00:04:30.600 --> 00:04:33.850
before we talk about whether or not
the "hit-and-run driver of D Hill" exists,

00:04:33.850 --> 00:04:37.480
it's starting to get sketchy on whether or
not the traffic accident happened at all.

00:04:37.480 --> 00:04:39.690
Huh? What does that mean?

00:04:41.110 --> 00:04:42.690
Are you saying it was all a sham?

00:04:43.900 --> 00:04:45.740
I don't want to say that.

00:04:45.740 --> 00:04:47.950
You're the scumbag
and you still made that face,

00:04:47.950 --> 00:04:51.160
so this shouldn't be a theory that
I can present to Nagahiro or our leader.

00:04:51.160 --> 00:04:55.330
B-But, even if there aren't any
eyewitnesses, there's a testimony, right?

00:04:55.670 --> 00:04:58.090
They said she got run over
while talking to a friend.

00:04:59.670 --> 00:05:03.130
But the friend didn't see
the car or anything.

00:05:03.130 --> 00:05:08.550
It's not that hard to have the friend listen to
a pre-recorded sound of a car to fake an accident.

00:05:08.550 --> 00:05:13.770
And ultimately, it's not impossible to talk it out
beforehand for a suitable testimony.

00:05:13.770 --> 00:05:16.650
It's not impossible, huh?

00:05:16.650 --> 00:05:18.560
That's right on target.

00:05:18.560 --> 00:05:22.190
This makes it normal for there
to be no evidence nor testimony.

00:05:22.190 --> 00:05:28.740
The problem is, why would Naganawa
have to go through this charade?

00:05:30.830 --> 00:05:33.120
If we're going to assume that it was a sham,

00:05:33.120 --> 00:05:36.500
I can only think of motives
that would make me sick to my stomach.

00:05:38.250 --> 00:05:42.050
The first thing that comes to mind
is "she dreaded it."

00:05:43.420 --> 00:05:47.300
But that's not really the first thing
that comes to mind, is it?

00:05:47.300 --> 00:05:49.220
By retiring from the campaign

00:05:49.220 --> 00:05:52.220
right before the election with the guise
of an unforeseen accident,

00:05:52.220 --> 00:05:56.270
she intended to interfere with
the continuation of the current regime.

00:05:56.270 --> 00:06:01.150
She plotted to ruin
Mr. Senpai's political ideas.

00:06:01.150 --> 00:06:04.860
For instance, by secretly communicating
with another candidate?

00:06:04.860 --> 00:06:08.360
The current top candidate is
Yokuya.

00:06:08.360 --> 00:06:13.830
If that's the case, I'd be convinced if she
was communicating with the academy instead.

00:06:13.830 --> 00:06:15.370
With the academy?

00:06:15.370 --> 00:06:20.500
We know that Nagahiro's political stance
was inconvenient for the academy.

00:06:20.500 --> 00:06:28.840
It would be easier to persuade the successor
instead of fighting the Nagahiro camp head-on.

00:06:31.090 --> 00:06:36.390
We need to go visit Naganawa once,
maybe as soon as tomorrow after school.

00:06:36.390 --> 00:06:38.230
Without telling Nagahiro.

00:06:39.390 --> 00:06:40.480
"OLDER BROTHER"

00:06:41.900 --> 00:06:44.270
We're going to go meet Mr. Odoru.

00:06:44.270 --> 00:06:45.690
"Mr. Odoru."

00:06:45.690 --> 00:06:47.690
Odoru Sotoin.

00:06:47.690 --> 00:06:49.820
The founder of
the Pretty Boy Detective Club.

00:06:49.820 --> 00:06:54.580
And the older brother of
the current leader, Manabu Sotoin.

00:06:54.580 --> 00:06:58.120
People called him "Odoru the Storyteller."

00:06:58.120 --> 00:07:02.500
At this rate, the campaign may drag on.

00:07:02.500 --> 00:07:06.210
I preferred not to do this,
but I decided to use an ace in the hole.

00:07:06.210 --> 00:07:09.510
So where exactly is Odoru?

00:07:09.510 --> 00:07:10.880
At the head of the school.

00:07:10.880 --> 00:07:12.930
Huh? Our leader's older brother
is in everyone's heads?

00:07:12.930 --> 00:07:15.310
"LOLI LOLI         "SCUM SCUM
DANCE"              ODORU"

00:07:12.930 --> 00:07:15.310
Huh? Our leader's older brother
is in everyone's heads?

00:07:15.430 --> 00:07:17.560
Not that head.

00:07:17.560 --> 00:07:20.020
Who are you calling a cerebral resident?

00:07:20.940 --> 00:07:24.440
I meant high school, as in Yubiwa Academy
High School. He's a second-year.

00:07:24.440 --> 00:07:27.360
D-Do you mean we're going to get advice

00:07:27.360 --> 00:07:30.360
from the original leader
of the Pretty Boy Detective Club?

00:07:30.360 --> 00:07:33.950
It's not about visiting Mr. Odoru,
our first leader,

00:07:33.950 --> 00:07:37.740
but more about visiting Mr. Odoru
the student council president before me.

00:07:37.740 --> 00:07:40.120
The previous student council president?

00:07:40.120 --> 00:07:41.040
Yes.

00:07:41.040 --> 00:07:45.420
Mr. Odoru is the legendary student council
president who the current third-years

00:07:45.420 --> 00:07:48.630
still talk about to this day.

00:07:48.630 --> 00:07:51.050
Someone who I can't even compare to.

00:07:53.930 --> 00:08:00.390
I was inadequate, and could not boost you
to the top with just my support.

00:08:00.390 --> 00:08:04.650
I figured we'll garner further support
from Mr. Odoru.

00:08:04.650 --> 00:08:09.110
Then wouldn't it be best if our leader came
along with us? After all, he's the younger--

00:08:09.110 --> 00:08:11.820
Our leader accompanying us won't happen.

00:08:12.990 --> 00:08:16.830
Can it be that the brothers don't get along?

00:08:16.830 --> 00:08:20.080
No, it's nothing like that.

00:08:20.080 --> 00:08:22.370
Well, you'll see when you meet him.

00:08:22.370 --> 00:08:23.290
"ODORU SOTOIN"

00:08:23.290 --> 00:08:26.750
"ODORU SOTOIN"
After all, he's the founder
of the Pretty Boy Detective Club.

00:08:26.750 --> 00:08:28.250
"YUBIWA"

00:08:26.750 --> 00:08:28.250
He's Odoru the Storyteller.

00:08:28.250 --> 00:08:29.250
"YUBIWA"

00:08:28.250 --> 00:08:29.250
Above anything else,
he's that leader's older brother.

00:08:29.250 --> 00:08:31.550
Above anything else,
he's that leader's older brother.

00:08:31.550 --> 00:08:34.380
I let my imagination run wild.

00:08:34.380 --> 00:08:38.220
However, this uneasiness
didn't really prove anything.

00:08:38.220 --> 00:08:40.930
In a bad way, it missed the bulls-eye.

00:08:40.930 --> 00:08:42.230
How do I put it?

00:08:43.560 --> 00:08:46.440
He was a smart-looking guy
in the normal sense.

00:08:46.440 --> 00:08:49.780
Nice to meet you. I'm Odoru Sotoin.

00:08:49.780 --> 00:08:51.610
So you must be Mayumi?

00:08:51.610 --> 00:08:53.740
I've heard about you from Sakiguchi.

00:08:53.740 --> 00:08:56.950
So you're running in
the student council presidential election?

00:08:56.950 --> 00:08:58.280
Best of luck.

00:08:58.280 --> 00:09:01.040
I'm sure there'd be no doubt
if Sakiguchi is endorsing you.

00:09:01.040 --> 00:09:04.040
You can use my name however you see fit.

00:09:04.040 --> 00:09:05.790
Oh, and give my regards
to my little brother.

00:09:05.790 --> 00:09:11.550
Can you tell him that he shouldn't be
spoiled by older boys and girls forever?

00:09:12.590 --> 00:09:14.090
He's so ordinary.

00:09:14.090 --> 00:09:17.640
He's plainly kind,
and an ordinary good guy.

00:09:17.640 --> 00:09:20.510
When you say he's our leader's
older brother, I can see it,

00:09:20.510 --> 00:09:25.100
and I do think the President
would look like this once he grows up.

00:09:25.100 --> 00:09:29.730
But more than the disappointment that I felt,
there was a sense that something was off.

00:09:29.730 --> 00:09:35.030
It felt like he was distancing himself in a way,
even with Mr. Senpai who he's known for a while.

00:09:35.030 --> 00:09:38.240
Awkward and standoffish.

00:09:38.240 --> 00:09:43.160
Um, so are you still on the student council
even in high school?

00:09:46.920 --> 00:09:49.000
Oh, no.

00:09:49.000 --> 00:09:52.800
I don't really do things like that anymore.

00:09:55.920 --> 00:10:00.300
He phrased it in such a way that
I didn't want to ask any further questions.

00:10:00.300 --> 00:10:03.390
It's like the era he spent as
the legendary student council president

00:10:03.390 --> 00:10:05.480
was something he was embarrassed about.

00:10:05.480 --> 00:10:08.230
As if I touched upon his past
of being a rash youngster.

00:10:10.270 --> 00:10:14.610
Sakiguchi, you've been helping me
by taking good care of my little brother,

00:10:14.610 --> 00:10:20.620
but you're about to enter high school,
so you should graduate from childish playtime.

00:10:20.620 --> 00:10:23.740
Well, yes.

00:10:23.740 --> 00:10:26.120
The fact that he was
a distinguished student council president,

00:10:26.120 --> 00:10:29.080
and the fact that he founded
the Pretty Boy Detective Club

00:10:29.080 --> 00:10:33.170
are all stories of the past for Odoru.

00:10:33.170 --> 00:10:35.840
It's not like he wants to pretend like
they never happened,

00:10:35.840 --> 00:10:40.590
but Odoru is no longer fighting the academy
with the administration's direction,

00:10:40.590 --> 00:10:45.220
and he doesn't think about trying to be pretty,
nor be a boy, nor be a detective.

00:10:45.220 --> 00:10:49.560
He's definitely an old friend,
but he's not part of the team.

00:10:49.560 --> 00:10:51.810
Why was he doing something like this?

00:10:51.810 --> 00:10:55.980
How important was it,
and just how irreplaceable was it?

00:10:55.980 --> 00:10:58.700
He can't remember any of that anymore.

00:10:58.700 --> 00:11:02.030
That's right. He's graduated from child's play.

00:11:02.030 --> 00:11:03.410
That's the thing.

00:11:03.410 --> 00:11:07.250
He was a person who always spoke
in song and dance.

00:11:07.250 --> 00:11:14.000
When he was around, the Pretty Boy
Detective Club really felt like a musical every day.

00:11:15.000 --> 00:11:16.920
Odoru the Storyteller.

00:11:16.920 --> 00:11:21.130
When he sings,
every case turned into an epic tale.

00:11:21.130 --> 00:11:24.760
Though it seems like he's given up
on both song and dance in high school.

00:11:24.760 --> 00:11:26.850
Why did he give them up?

00:11:26.850 --> 00:11:29.140
He mentioned something about
his studies getting busier,

00:11:29.140 --> 00:11:33.860
and also because he learned
how high the national level was.

00:11:33.860 --> 00:11:36.570
But I don't know what really happened.

00:11:36.570 --> 00:11:40.490
For now, I'm cruising as
a scummy character as you can see,

00:11:40.490 --> 00:11:44.530
but once I enter high school,
will I forget I did all of this?

00:11:44.530 --> 00:11:49.960
Your scumminess is a lifelong thing, so I
don't think you need to worry about that.

00:11:49.960 --> 00:11:54.460
Growth, evolution,
rehabilitation, full maturity.

00:11:54.460 --> 00:12:00.550
Scumminess aside, I don't think I would still be
cross-dressing as a second-year in high school.

00:12:00.550 --> 00:12:03.300
It's for a limited time,
and something transient.

00:12:03.300 --> 00:12:06.350
That is, in fact, child's play.

00:12:06.350 --> 00:12:09.560
An amusement that you're always
bound to graduate from someday.

00:12:13.310 --> 00:12:15.650
Mr. Odoru Sotoin.

00:12:15.650 --> 00:12:20.030
The past aside, he's currently an ordinary
second-year in high school.

00:12:20.030 --> 00:12:23.280
Indeed. That's what normal is.

00:12:23.280 --> 00:12:25.070
Normal.

00:12:25.070 --> 00:12:27.410
If that's what normal is...

00:12:27.410 --> 00:12:32.330
Kinshiro Yokuya may seem like
run-of-the-mill and un-individualistic,

00:12:32.330 --> 00:12:34.370
but by no means is he normal.

00:12:34.370 --> 00:12:36.460
He's far from normal.

00:12:38.050 --> 00:12:40.010
"ON THE WAY TO THE HOSPITAL"

00:12:40.260 --> 00:12:43.050
Thanks to the announcement that
not only do I have the endorsement

00:12:43.050 --> 00:12:47.680
of the current student council president,
but also the support from the previous president,

00:12:47.680 --> 00:12:50.600
"FIRST - KINSHIRO YOKUYA
SECOND - MAYUMI DOJIMA"

00:12:47.680 --> 00:12:50.600
my projected approval rating
by the school newspaper

00:12:50.600 --> 00:12:54.060
"FIRST - KINSHIRO YOKUYA
SECOND - MAYUMI DOJIMA"

00:12:50.600 --> 00:12:54.060
instantly jumped to
second place that day.

00:12:54.060 --> 00:12:56.560
"SECOND PLACE"

00:12:54.060 --> 00:12:56.560
But even with all that, second place.

00:12:56.810 --> 00:12:59.070
I needed one more decisive move.

00:12:59.070 --> 00:13:04.070
"MAYUMI DOJIMA
A SHINING VISION"

00:12:59.070 --> 00:13:04.070
This may or may not become that decisive move,
or this might even create the reverse effect.

00:13:04.070 --> 00:13:06.780
"MAYUMI DOJIMA
A SHINING VISION"

00:13:04.070 --> 00:13:06.780
Headwind or tailwind, I paired up
with Mr. Delinquent after school

00:13:06.780 --> 00:13:08.830
Headwind or tailwind, I paired up
with Mr. Delinquent after school

00:13:08.830 --> 00:13:14.080
and headed to the hospital where Naganawa,
the original candidate, was staying.

00:13:14.080 --> 00:13:16.040
Wait for us, Naganawa.

00:13:16.040 --> 00:13:18.290
A delinquent and a scum
is about to visit you!

00:13:18.290 --> 00:13:21.050
When you say it that way,
we're a preposterous pair.

00:13:22.760 --> 00:13:26.840
Come to think, have you ever met Odoru?

00:13:26.840 --> 00:13:30.260
I've met him a couple times
while interacting with our leader.

00:13:30.260 --> 00:13:35.230
But by the time I met him,
he'd already reformed his life by a lot.

00:13:35.230 --> 00:13:38.270
They say, "I've become such a dull adult."

00:13:38.270 --> 00:13:43.690
But that "dull adult" must think of his
past self as "what a dull child I was."

00:13:43.690 --> 00:13:48.700
Well, when you think about it, it might be wrong
to call a second-year in high school an adult.

00:13:49.070 --> 00:13:51.240
But I think the current Odoru

00:13:51.240 --> 00:13:56.920
has definitely lost his boyishness,
and what made him a pretty boy.

00:13:56.920 --> 00:14:00.920
Isn't "lost" a one-sided opinion, too?

00:14:00.920 --> 00:14:04.970
From his point of view, this just means
he "gained" something new.

00:14:04.970 --> 00:14:10.010
Don't worry.
You'll stay as a scum forever and always.

00:14:11.260 --> 00:14:15.930
And maybe you'll reform yourself pretty
easily once you're in high school, too.

00:14:15.930 --> 00:14:21.060
Then you'll say tacky things like "I used to be
this bossman, causing a lot of mischief."

00:14:21.060 --> 00:14:25.860
Oh, but I'm not sure
if I'll go to high school.

00:14:27.450 --> 00:14:30.870
Anyways, Mayumi, about the D Hill case.

00:14:30.870 --> 00:14:35.370
I wanted to make sure, so I snuck out of school
during lunch break and took another look.

00:14:35.370 --> 00:14:37.710
Wh-What did you just say?

00:14:37.710 --> 00:14:42.290
I said, I snuck out of school during
lunch break and inspected the scene again.

00:14:42.290 --> 00:14:44.710
As they say,
"Look at the scene a hundred times."

00:14:44.710 --> 00:14:47.510
You know how that place
is an uphill one-way street?

00:14:48.510 --> 00:14:50.010
Um, yeah.

00:14:50.010 --> 00:14:53.060
Naganawa got run over
on her way home from school,

00:14:53.060 --> 00:14:57.980
so of course she was walking downhill
on the sidewalk, right?

00:14:57.980 --> 00:15:03.070
The vector of Naganawa going downhill
and the vector of the car going uphill

00:15:03.070 --> 00:15:06.400
pass each other head-on
until she crosses the crosswalk.

00:15:06.400 --> 00:15:10.910
Then, wouldn't she have had clear
visual confirmation of the oncoming car?

00:15:10.910 --> 00:15:13.780
That's a possibility we hadn't thought of.

00:15:13.780 --> 00:15:17.000
Because the crosswalk cuts
across the road,

00:15:17.000 --> 00:15:21.580
we kept imagining scenes
of the incoming impact from the side,

00:15:21.580 --> 00:15:26.050
but if we rewound time just a little bit,
Naganawa's line of sight as she walks downhill

00:15:26.050 --> 00:15:29.880
would be in a position that would see
the car driving uphill head-on.

00:15:29.880 --> 00:15:32.760
If she was able to see
the car coming uphill,

00:15:32.760 --> 00:15:38.350
wouldn't you think she would stop regardless
of the crosswalk signal being red or green?

00:15:38.350 --> 00:15:40.020
But of course.

00:15:40.020 --> 00:15:46.020
The driver would have been able to see
Naganawa without any obstruction as well.

00:15:46.020 --> 00:15:49.320
Because it's D Hill that has few
pedestrians and low vehicle traffic,

00:15:49.320 --> 00:15:51.780
I thought it would be easy
for a hit-and-run.

00:15:51.780 --> 00:15:55.620
But if you think about it thoroughly, you realize
that's why it's hard for an accident to occur.

00:15:55.620 --> 00:15:58.200
It's not a location fit
to make it look like an accident either.

00:15:58.200 --> 00:16:04.080
Even if you were targeting someone intentionally,
it's not a location that's highly likely to fail.

00:16:04.080 --> 00:16:07.590
Then what kind of
location is it fit to be?

00:16:07.590 --> 00:16:09.590
A location that doesn't
make it seem like an accident,

00:16:09.590 --> 00:16:11.970
but a location that makes it seem like
there was an accident.

00:16:13.010 --> 00:16:14.890
Hey, Mr. Delinquent.

00:16:14.890 --> 00:16:19.930
If Naganawa really was a traitor,
what will you do?

00:16:19.930 --> 00:16:22.980
Would you tell
Mr. Senpai or our leader about it?

00:16:22.980 --> 00:16:24.900
Of course I wouldn't tell them.

00:16:26.020 --> 00:16:28.530
I'll take it to my grave.

00:16:28.530 --> 00:16:30.860
It would be a life-long secret
just between us.

00:16:31.820 --> 00:16:33.910
You'll need to win the election on your own.

00:16:33.910 --> 00:16:35.370
"AS VICE-PRESIDENT"

00:16:38.240 --> 00:16:40.410
W-Welcome?

00:16:40.410 --> 00:16:42.370
Th-Thank you?

00:16:42.870 --> 00:16:46.340
She didn't seem like a Snow Queen,
nor like the vice-president.

00:16:46.340 --> 00:16:50.090
Well, I can kind of understand
why Fukuroi would be here.

00:16:50.090 --> 00:16:53.630
But who in the world are you?

00:16:55.050 --> 00:16:58.310
I think I've seen you before.
You're in Class B.

00:16:58.310 --> 00:17:00.180
Whoa, she knew about me.

00:17:00.180 --> 00:17:01.770
It wouldn't be strange

00:17:01.770 --> 00:17:05.980
for a student council member to know about
a mysterious cross-dressing girl.

00:17:05.980 --> 00:17:08.820
And someone who has
a great interest in the stars.

00:17:08.820 --> 00:17:10.780
She knew about me
from before my cross-dressing.

00:17:10.780 --> 00:17:13.150
I see. She's quite competent.

00:17:13.150 --> 00:17:17.200
I'm Mayumi Dojima.
The thing is, Mr. Senp...

00:17:17.200 --> 00:17:20.200
Um, I was asked
by President Sakiguchi to say hello.

00:17:20.200 --> 00:17:26.460
Oh, I see. So you must be Miss Dojima
who decided to run in my place.

00:17:26.460 --> 00:17:27.540
Thank you!

00:17:30.420 --> 00:17:33.470
This is perfect.
There's something I wanted to give you.

00:17:33.470 --> 00:17:39.180
Well, I thought this might be too much,
but I wanted to help you in some way.

00:17:39.180 --> 00:17:41.930
I compiled all the work I did
as vice-president,

00:17:41.930 --> 00:17:46.230
and made scrapbooks from
previous issues of the school paper.

00:17:46.230 --> 00:17:49.400
Please take it home if you'd like.

00:17:49.400 --> 00:17:51.190
Hey, look at me.

00:17:51.190 --> 00:17:53.740
We came here because you mentioned it.

00:17:53.740 --> 00:17:59.070
To think that the girl feared as the Snow Queen
would approach me in such a friendly manner.

00:17:59.070 --> 00:18:01.870
And she's quite cooperative.

00:18:01.870 --> 00:18:03.080
Fukuroi.

00:18:03.080 --> 00:18:05.080
I've gone through a lot with you,

00:18:05.080 --> 00:18:09.250
but if you'll help us with this election,
then let's have a temporary cease-fire.

00:18:09.250 --> 00:18:11.300
Oh yeah, I guess so.

00:18:13.460 --> 00:18:16.340
There's something I want to ask you.

00:18:16.340 --> 00:18:20.800
Can you tell us about the accident?

00:18:20.800 --> 00:18:24.390
Rule Three. Be a Detective.

00:18:24.390 --> 00:18:26.390
About the accident?

00:18:26.390 --> 00:18:29.650
Fukuroi, why do you want
to hear about that?

00:18:29.650 --> 00:18:33.360
D-Don't worry about it! We're just
asking everyone who was involved!

00:18:33.360 --> 00:18:36.990
Crap! That's a stock phrase you use
when you're asking about alibis!

00:18:36.990 --> 00:18:39.410
One of her campaign pledges

00:18:39.410 --> 00:18:44.290
is to increase the safety of school
routes used for student commutes.

00:18:44.290 --> 00:18:47.330
Sakiguchi the incumbent president
had thoughts to clear away

00:18:47.330 --> 00:18:50.630
any worries that you might have,
even just a little bit.

00:18:50.630 --> 00:18:56.720
Mr. Delinquent, I had believed you were someone
who was faithful and unable to tell lies.

00:18:56.720 --> 00:18:59.130
I'll never trust you again.

00:18:59.130 --> 00:19:01.180
Oh, I see.

00:19:01.180 --> 00:19:06.850
But I also told Sakiguchi that I don't really
remember anything when it happened.

00:19:06.850 --> 00:19:09.980
I don't remember the car make
or the license plate,

00:19:09.980 --> 00:19:15.900
let alone why I decided to take D Hill
on my way home that day.

00:19:15.900 --> 00:19:20.030
If I used my usual school route,
this wouldn't have happened.

00:19:20.030 --> 00:19:23.910
That means you usually don't use D Hill?

00:19:23.910 --> 00:19:29.290
Right. Unless I'm in a real hurry,
or have some special reason to use it.

00:19:29.290 --> 00:19:34.550
So was she in quite the hurry
or was it a special circumstance?

00:19:34.550 --> 00:19:38.010
Either way, as we continued
the interrogation,

00:19:38.010 --> 00:19:42.890
we investigators had to admit that
the possibility of a sham or a charade

00:19:42.890 --> 00:19:48.600
for the traffic accident at D Hill
was exceedingly difficult.

00:19:48.600 --> 00:19:53.150
We had to call off all allegations
against Naganawa.

00:19:54.570 --> 00:19:57.570
We had to clean the slate.

00:19:57.570 --> 00:19:59.530
"RETURNING FROM THE HOSPITAL"

00:19:59.860 --> 00:20:05.120
Well, Mr. Delinquent, as we promised,
let's take this visitation to our graves.

00:20:05.120 --> 00:20:06.740
It's a secret just between us.

00:20:06.740 --> 00:20:10.080
That was only if our hunch was correct.

00:20:10.080 --> 00:20:14.590
We're going to report this to our leader,
and make sure our stories are consistent.

00:20:14.590 --> 00:20:17.170
Vice-president totally won you over, huh?

00:20:18.590 --> 00:20:22.510
If we determined that Naganawa
ended up being the traitor,

00:20:22.510 --> 00:20:26.180
we had the possibility of daisy-chaining
things to the mastermind.

00:20:27.100 --> 00:20:29.850
But such a mastermind didn't exist.

00:20:29.850 --> 00:20:33.480
At least, there wasn't
one behind Naganawa.

00:20:34.770 --> 00:20:37.270
But I wasn't paying attention.

00:20:37.270 --> 00:20:41.650
The fact that such a mastermind didn't
exist means that at the end of the day,

00:20:41.650 --> 00:20:46.200
we couldn't strike out the possibility that
the "hit-and-run driver of D Hill" exists.

00:20:46.200 --> 00:20:47.330
In other words...

00:20:47.330 --> 00:20:50.500
...as a substitute candidate for Naganawa,

00:20:50.500 --> 00:20:56.540
there's still the possibility
that I'll be targeted by a car.

00:20:56.540 --> 00:20:58.590
I'd forgotten about that.

00:21:02.930 --> 00:21:05.470
It was clearly targeting me.

00:21:08.850 --> 00:21:10.470
Mayumi! Check its plates!

00:21:16.480 --> 00:21:18.110
Probatio diabolica.

00:21:19.860 --> 00:21:26.370
So the devil and "hit-and-run driver of
D Hill" both existed. That much is clear.

00:21:26.370 --> 00:21:28.870
But who in the world...

00:21:28.870 --> 00:21:31.120
That was made clear, too.

00:21:38.630 --> 00:21:41.090
Even while flying through the air,

00:21:41.090 --> 00:21:45.260
I got visual confirmation of the car
targeting me with my naked eyes.

00:21:45.260 --> 00:21:52.020
I also caught a clear glimpse of the driver's face
who held the wheel behind the smoked glass.

00:21:52.020 --> 00:21:53.520
And it was...

00:21:53.520 --> 00:21:55.640
...a face that I was familiar with.

00:21:55.640 --> 00:21:58.190
A face I recognized.

00:21:58.190 --> 00:21:59.020
It was the un-individualistic one
sitting next to me in class.

00:21:59.020 --> 00:22:00.690
"HIT-AND-RUN DRIVER"

00:21:59.020 --> 00:22:00.690
It was the un-individualistic one
sitting next to me in class.

00:22:00.690 --> 00:22:02.440
"WITNESSING THE HIT-AND-RUN DRIVER"

00:22:00.690 --> 00:22:02.440
It was the un-individualistic one
sitting next to me in class.

00:22:02.440 --> 00:22:05.950
"EPISODE 11
THE PRETTY BOY ON D HILL (PART 2)"
